This Law defines the legal, economic, and organizational principles for the implementation of state policy in the field of public employment, state guarantees for the protection of citizens' rights to work and the realization of their rights to social protection against unemployment.

#### Chapter I GENERAL PROVISIONS

##### Article 1. Definition of terms

##### 1. In this Law, the terms are used in the following sense:

1) unemployment is a socio-economic phenomenon, in which part of the people is unable to exercise their right to work and receive wages (remuneration) as a source of livelihood;

2) unemployed - a person aged from 15 to 70 who, due to lack of work, does not have earnings or other sources of income provided for by law as a source of livelihood, is ready and able to start work;

3) vacancy - a vacant position (job) for which a person can be employed;

4) voucher - a document of the established model, which gives a person, in accordance with this Law, the right to retraining in a labor profession, training in a specialty to obtain a master's degree based on a bachelor's or master's degree obtained in another specialty, training at the next level of education (except for the third ( educational-scientific/educational-creative) level of higher education), specialization and advanced training in educational institutions or at the employer;

__

1 4 ) seconded foreign workers - foreigners and stateless persons sent by a foreign employer to Ukraine to perform a certain amount of work (services) on the basis of agreements (contracts) concluded between Ukrainian and foreign business entities;

1 __

5) freely chosen employment - realization of a citizen's right to freely choose a type of activity not prohibited by law (in particular, one that is not related to the performance of paid work), as well as a profession and place of work in accordance with one's abilities and needs;

### About population employment

1 5 ) intra-corporate assignees - foreigners and stateless persons recognized as such in accordance with the schedule of specific obligations in the services sector of the Protocol on Ukraine's Accession to the World Trade Organization ( Article II of the General Agreement on Trade in Services);

1 __

6) state regulation of employment - formation and implementation of state policy in the field of population employment with the aim of creating conditions for ensuring full and productive freely chosen employment and social protection in the event of unemployment;

7) employment - the activity of persons not prohibited by law, related to the satisfaction of their personal and social needs with the aim of receiving income (salary) in monetary or other form, as well as the activity of members of the same family who carry out economic activities or work in business entities based on their property, including free of charge;

8) registered unemployed person - a person of working age who is registered in the territorial body of the central executive body that implements the state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration as unemployed and ready and able to start work;

