3 8 ) foreign employee - a foreigner or stateless person who works under an employment contract with a Ukrainian employer in accordance with the legislation of Ukraine;

3 __

4 __

9) employee competitiveness - a set of qualities of a person characterizing his ability to work, the level of knowledge, skills and abilities;

__

11) part-time employment - employment of an employee under the conditions of working hours, which is less than the standard time provided by the law, and can be established under a contract between the employee and the employer with remuneration in proportion to the time worked or depending on the output;

12) new workplace - a workplace created in connection with the creation of a new economic entity (except for the one created by termination) or an increase in the number of employees, provided that there is no reduction (decrease) in the average monthly number of employees for the previous 12 months, and also created by modernization or change of production technology, which require new knowledge, skills and abilities of the employee;

### About population employment

13) persons of working age - persons over the age of 16 who have not reached the retirement age established by Article 26 of the Law of Ukraine "On Mandatory State Pension Insurance" ;

14) full-time employment - employment of an employee according to the norm of working hours provided for in accordance with legislation, a collective or labor agreement;

15) employment - a set of legal, economic and organizational measures aimed at ensuring the realization of a person's right to work;

16) able-bodied persons - persons over the age of 16 who live on the territory of Ukraine and are capable of active labor due to their health;

17) productive employment - employment that makes it possible to ensure effective social production and satisfy the needs of the employee at the level of at least the guarantees established by law;

18) professional training - acquisition and improvement of professional knowledge, abilities and skills of a person in accordance with his abilities, which ensures the appropriate level of professional qualification for professional activity and competitiveness in the labor market;

19) labor market - a system of legal, social, labor, economic and organizational relations that arise between job seekers, employees, trade unions, employers and their organizations, state authorities in the field of meeting the needs of employees in employment, and employers - in hiring employees in accordance with the legislation;

20) workplace - a place (premises) where an employee is permanently or temporarily in the process of work and which is determined, in particular, on the basis of an employment contract (contract);

21) social protection in the event of unemployment - a set of measures provided for by the mandatory state social insurance in case of unemployment and the legislation on population employment;

22) a business entity that provides employment mediation services is a legal entity registered in accordance with the procedure established by law, which conducts economic activity, regardless of the form of ownership, type of activity and management, as well as a natural person - an entrepreneur that provides services with mediation in employment in Ukraine and/or abroad in accordance with this Law and other acts of legislation;

23) labor migration - movement of a person associated with crossing the state border or borders of an administrative-territorial unit for the purpose of performing or finding work;

### Article 5. Guarantees in the field of public employment

1. The state guarantees in the field of employment:

1) free choice of place of employment and type of activity, free choice or change of profession;

- 2) receiving wages (remuneration) in accordance with legislation;

- 3) professional orientation for the purpose of self-determination and realization of a person's

- ability to work;

4) professional training in accordance with abilities and taking into account the needs of the labor market;

5) confirmation of the results of informal professional training of persons in working professions;

6) free assistance in finding a job, choosing a suitable job and obtaining information about the situation on the labor market and prospects for its development;

- 7) social protection in case of unemployment;

- 8) protection against discrimination in the field of employment, unjustified refusal to hire and

- illegal dismissal;

- 9) additional assistance in employment of certain categories of citizens.

### Article 9. The right of a person to social protection in case of unemployment

1. Everyone has the right to social protection in the event of unemployment, which is implemented through:

1) participation in the mandatory state social insurance in the event of unemployment, which provides financial support in the event of unemployment;

2) provision of free social services, in particular, information and consultation and career guidance, professional training, retraining, advanced training taking into account the demand on the labor market, assistance in employment, in particular, through financial support for self-employment and the implementation of entrepreneurial initiatives in accordance with legislation;

3) provision of special guarantees to employees who lost their jobs due to changes in the organization of production and labor;

4) providing an additional guarantee of employment to certain categories of the population who are unable to compete on equal terms in the labor market.

### Article 14. Categories of citizens with additional guarantees in promoting employment

1. The categories of citizens who have additional guarantees in promoting employment include:

1) one of the parents or a person replacing them and:

has dependent child(ren) under the age of six;

__

raises a child under the age of 14 or a child with a disability without one of the spouses;

maintains without one of the spouses a person with a disability since childhood (regardless of age) and/or a person with a disability of the I group (regardless of the cause of disability);

2) orphans and children deprived of parental care;

__

3) persons released after serving a sentence or forced treatment;

4) young people who have completed or stopped studying in institutions of general secondary, professional (vocational-technical), professional pre-higher and higher education, have been released from fixed-term military or alternative (non-military) service, military service by conscription of reservists in a special period ( within six months after the end or termination of education or service) and who is hired for the first time;

__

5) persons who have 10 or less years left before the right to an old-age pension in accordance with Article 26 of the Law of Ukraine "On Mandatory State Pension Insurance" ;

6) persons with disabilities who have not reached the retirement age established by Article 26 of the Law of Ukraine "On Mandatory State Pension Insurance" ;

7) persons who have reached the age of 15 and who, with the consent of one of their parents or a person who replaces them, can, as an exception, be hired;

8) participants in hostilities specified in clauses 19-21 of the first part of Article 6 of the Law of Ukraine "On the status of war veterans, guarantees of their social protection;

__

9) unemployed able-bodied persons who receive state social assistance to low-income families;

