Article 33. Professional orientation of persons who applied to the territorial bodies of the central executive body implementing the state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration

1. Professional orientation of persons who have applied to the territorial bodies of the central executive body, which implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, is carried out by:

1) professional information, which consists in providing information about labor activity and its role in the professional self-determination of a person, information about the state of the labor market, the content and prospects for the development of modern professions, qualifications, skills, types, forms and conditions of vocational training, opportunities for professional qualification and career growth, which will contribute to the formation of professional interests, intentions and motivation of a person regarding the choice or change of the type of work, profession, qualification, work, type and form of professional training, development of skills and acquisition of new competencies;

__

2) professional counseling aimed at optimizing a person's professional self-determination based on the identification of his individual psychological characteristics, peculiarities of life situations, professional interests, inclinations, state of health and taking into account the needs of the labor market;

