### Article 34. Professional training

5. In case of refusal of the employee or other person to work for the employer during the period agreed with him, dismissal from work before the end of such period, the employee or other person is obliged to reimburse the employer for the expenses related to the payment of training, or a part of them, in proportion to the period worked for conditions determined by the contract. An employee or other person is not obliged to reimburse the employer for the costs related to training, if they did not start work or were dismissed from work for the following reasons:

1) establishment of disability;

2) dismissal at the initiative of the employer, which is not related to the employee committing illegal actions;

3) conscription for military service or referral to alternative (non-military) service;

4) on his own initiative in connection with the employer's violation of labor legislation, collective agreements, a collective or labor contract;

5) care for a child with a disability and (or) a person with a disability of the I group (regardless of the cause of the disability).

6. The procedure for confirming the results of informal professional training of persons in labor professions is determined by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.

### Article 36. Activities of business entities that provide employment mediation services

1) knowingly recruiting, employing or hiring workers for work involving unacceptable dangers and risks, as well as for work in which these workers may become victims of abuse or discrimination of any nature;

2) prevent the employer from hiring the involved employee directly, limit the employee's professional mobility, impose sanctions on the employee who agreed to work for another employer;

3) provide employees at the disposal of the employer to replace his employees who are on strike or other collective actions.

### Article 37. Activities of business entities that provide employment mediation services in Ukraine

1. Business entities that provide employment mediation services in Ukraine cooperate with territorial bodies of the central executive body that implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, by:

1) conclusion of agreements on cooperation in certain areas of activity, including for the exchange of data on vacant jobs (vacancies);

2) conducting joint events (projects);

3) consulting with the aim of improving professional practice and providing services to employers and job seekers, including those with additional guarantees in the promotion of employment.

2. Business entities that provide employment mediation services in Ukraine are prohibited from receiving fees, commissions, and other rewards from citizens who have been provided with these services. Payment for employment services is made exclusively by the employer to whom such services were provided.

### Article 38. Activities of business entities providing employment mediation services abroad

1. A business entity has the right to provide employment mediation services abroad after its inclusion in the list of business entities providing employment mediation services abroad, and within the framework of concluded foreign economic agreements. Inclusion in such a list is carried out on the basis of a declaration submitted to the central executive body, which ensures the formation and implementation of state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, on the implementation of economic activity in the field of mediation in employment abroad in accordance with the procedure established by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.

2. In order to start the activity of providing mediation services in employment abroad and to be included in the list of business entities that provide mediation services in employment abroad, such business entity must:

1) to be registered in accordance with the procedure established by law for the type of economic activity of mediation in employment;

2) have a foreign economic agreement (contract) concluded with a foreign employer on the provision of mediation services in employment, search and selection of employees (hereinafter referred to as a foreign economic agreement (contract) and registration documents of a foreign business entity - employer in the country of location;

3) have a registered place of business activity;

4) submit a declaration on conducting business activities in the field of mediation in employment abroad.

3. Mediation services in employment abroad are provided by business entities in accordance with the concluded foreign economic agreement (contract).

The foreign economic agreement (contract) is concluded in the Ukrainian language and one or more languages used in the state of the employer's location.

The foreign economic agreement (contract) is kept by the business entity that provides mediation services in employment abroad for three years after its expiration.

4. An economic entity providing mediation services in employment abroad is obliged to:

1) to provide the citizen before leaving for employment abroad:

information in written form about the rights and guarantees granted to him under the employment contract (contract), provided for by the legislation of Ukraine and the legislation of the state of the employer's location;

contact details of consular institutions of Ukraine in the host country;

a draft employment contract (contract), certified by a foreign employer.

### Article 38. Activities of business entities providing employment mediation services abroad

Receipt of information and a draft of the employment contract (contract) is confirmed by a citizen's written (electronic digital) signature. The specified documents are kept by the business entity that provides mediation services in employment abroad for five years;

2) keep records of citizens who are employed abroad through his mediation;

3) to provide free of charge information and consultations to citizens about the advantages of legal employment abroad, the nature of future work, conditions and amount of remuneration, conditions of residence in the host country, the existence of international contracts (agreements) in the field of employment and social security concluded between Ukraine and the host country employer;

4) submit to the central body of executive power, which ensures the formation and implementation of state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, reporting on the implementation of activities for the provision of mediation services in employment abroad. The procedure , form and terms of submission of such reporting are approved by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine;

5) to notify the central body of executive power, which ensures the formation and implementation of state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, about a change in the data specified in the list of business entities that provide mediation services in employment abroad, within one month from the occurrence of such a change;

6) in the case of concluding new or several foreign economic agreements (contracts), information about them and registration documents of such foreign business entities - employers in the state of location are sent to the central body of executive power, which ensures the formation and implementation of state policy in the sphere of population employment and labor migrations, within a month after their conclusion;

7) to ensure unimpeded access to the registered place of business activity for the provision of mediation services in employment abroad for representatives of the central executive authority, which implements state policy on matters of supervision and control over compliance with legislation on labor and population employment, for the purpose of state control.

### Article 38. Activities of business entities providing employment mediation services abroad

The basis for making a decision on exclusion from the list of business entities that provide mediation services in employment abroad is:

1) statement of a business entity that provides mediation services in employment abroad, on exclusion from the list of business entities that provide mediation services in employment abroad;

2) availability in the Unified State Register of Legal Entities, Individual Entrepreneurs and Public Organizations of information on the state registration of the termination of a legal entity or the state registration of the termination of the business activity of an individual entrepreneur;

3) submission of a copy of the death certificate of a natural person - an entrepreneur;

4) non-submission or violation of the deadlines for submission of reports, provided for in clause 4 of part four of this article, during three consecutive reporting periods;

5) an act of the central executive body that implements state policy on matters of supervision and control over compliance with legislation on labor and employment of the population, drawn up based on the results of a state control measure in connection with non-fulfillment of the requirements for the elimination of violations provided for in parts four and six of this articles;

6) establishing the fact of providing mediation services in employment abroad without a concluded foreign economic agreement (contract);

7) impossibility of carrying out by the central body of the executive power, which implements the state policy on matters of supervision and control of compliance with the legislation on labor, employment of the population, checks on the specified in the list of business entities that provide mediation services in employment abroad, at the place of economic proceedings activities for the provision of mediation services in employment abroad within six months from the date specified in the decision on the inspection;

8) establishment of a person in the prescribed manner as a victim of human trafficking as a result of employment with the assistance of a business entity that provides mediation services in employment abroad.

