### Article 39. Activities of business entities that hire employees for their further work in Ukraine for another employer

1. Business entities - employers who hire employees for their further work in Ukraine for another employer, send employees under the conditions, if this is stipulated in the collective agreement of such an employer, and with the consent of the primary trade union organization, and are obliged to:

1) conclude a contract with the employer on the employment of the employee;

2) to pay the employee a salary in an amount not lower than the amount of the minimum wage established by law and the salary that the employee receives from the employer for performing the same work;

3) provide the employee with work and rest time under the conditions determined for the employer's employees, which is provided for by the terms of the collective agreement and the rules of internal labor regulations;

4) calculate and pay a single contribution to mandatory state social insurance for the benefit of the employee;

5) not to prevent the conclusion of an employment contract between the employee and the employer for whom he performed work.

