### Article 46. Suitable work for the unemployed

##### 1. A job that simultaneously:

1) corresponds to his education, profession/professions (specialties/specialties), qualification, as well as work experience acquired by the person during his employment. When offering a suitable job, the duration of work by profession (the profession of the corresponding group if there are skills), specialty, qualification, experience, duration of unemployment, as well as the need of the labor market are taken into account;

2) takes into account the transport accessibility established by the order of the head of the local state administration or the decision of the executive body of the relevant council. A job is considered suitable if the travel time and distance to the place of work (one-way), where daily transportation is organized, for the unemployed who are employed under the following conditions:

full-time - does not exceed an hour and a half and 60 kilometers;

part-time - does not exceed one hour and 40 kilometers;

3) corresponds to the wage level depending on the duration of unemployment. When selecting a suitable job, the following salary is taken into account:

not lower than the amount of salary (income, financial support) at the last place of work (service), and for persons who are in the status of registered unemployed - within 90 calendar days from the date of granting the status of registered unemployed;

60 percent of the salary (income, financial support) at the last place of work (service) - for persons who are in the status of registered unemployed from the 91st to the 180th calendar day;

minimum wage for full-time work (day) for persons who:

are unemployed for more than 180 calendar days;

wish to resume work after a long (more than 12 months) break;

search for work for the first time;

while being in the status of registered unemployed, received a new profession at the direction of the territorial body of the central executive body, which implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration (according to the received new profession).

### Article 47. Assistance for partial unemployment

1. Partial unemployment benefit is a type of state support for insured persons (employees and natural persons - entrepreneurs) in case they lose a part of their salary (income) in connection with the stop (reduction) of production (performance of work, provision of services) with reasons of an economic or technological nature, the emergence of an emergency situation, the introduction of a state of emergency or martial law, the establishment of quarantine.

Partial unemployment benefits are not provided to employees of state authorities, local selfgovernment bodies or institutions, institutions, organizations created by them in accordance with the established procedure, which are fully supported at the expense of the state or local budget.

2. Partial unemployment benefit is provided by the territorial body of the central executive body that implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, at the request of an employer or an individual entrepreneur who is an insured person, for its payment to employees or an individual entrepreneur, who is an insured person.

##### 3. Partial unemployment benefit is not provided if:

1) stoppage (reduction) of production (execution of works, provision of services) is seasonal in nature or occurs exclusively for organizational and production reasons;

2) the employee refused employment (temporary transfer) to a suitable full-time (weekly) job with the employer, or works for the employer part-time, or undergoes alternative (non-military) service;

3) during the six months preceding the month of stoppage (reduction) of production (execution of work, provision of services), the employer, natural person - entrepreneur has debts for the payment of wages and/or for the payment of a single contribution to the mandatory state social insurance , and/or from payment of insurance premiums for mandatory state pension insurance;

4) an employer, a natural person - an entrepreneur is in the process of termination of a legal entity, termination of business activity, has been declared bankrupt in accordance with the established procedure or a bankruptcy case has been initiated against him, is in the process of rehabilitation.

### Article 50. Participation of employers in ensuring employment of the population

1. The rights and obligations of employers and their associations with regard to ensuring the employment of the population, protection against unemployment and its consequences are determined by this Law, the laws of Ukraine "On employers' organizations, their associations, rights and guarantees of their activities" and "On social dialogue in Ukraine" , other normative legal acts, collective agreements and agreements concluded at the national, branch and regional levels.

