2. Employers participate in the implementation of measures to ensure the employment of the population by:

1) creation of conditions for citizens to exercise the right to work;

2) compliance with the requirements of the legislation on labor, population employment and mandatory state social insurance in case of unemployment;

3) approval of the content of professional training;

4) exercising the right to choose educational institutions, enterprises, institutions and organizations for professional training of the unemployed in accordance with the established requirements;

5) participation in state qualification attestation, state attestation of persons based on the results of professional training and confirmation of professional qualifications for labor professions of persons wishing to confirm the results of informal training;

6) submission of proposals to draft legislation on employment and labor migration;

7) participation in monitoring compliance with legislation in the field of population employment, labor migration, professional training and confirmation of employee qualifications.

3. Employers are obliged to:

1) to ensure decent working conditions that meet the requirements of legislation in the field of wages, occupational health and safety;

2) take measures to prevent mass layoffs, including through consultations with trade unions in order to develop appropriate measures aimed at mitigating their consequences and reducing the number of laid-off workers.

### Article 50. Participation of employers in ensuring employment of the population

For this purpose, the employer, in the course of consultations, but no later than three months before the date of possible layoffs, submits to the elected body of the primary trade union organization (trade union representative) a notice of planned mass layoffs with relevant information (in writing) about such measures, including information about the reasons subsequent layoffs, the average number and categories of employees, as well as the number and categories of employees that may be affected, and the timing of the layoffs. If there are several primary trade union organizations, the notification is sent to a joint representative body formed by them on the basis of proportional representation, and in the absence of such a body - to the elected body of the primary trade union organization (trade union representative), which unites the majority of employees of this employer. The procedure for conducting such consultations and implementing recommendations is determined by the collective agreement, and in its absence - by agreement.

In the case of dismissal of employees in accordance with clause 6 of part one of Article 41 of the Labor Code of Ukraine, the employer shall provide primary trade union organizations with information on these measures, including information on the reasons for dismissal, the number and categories of employees, no later than 10 calendar days before the planned dismissal of employees it may refer to the timing of dismissal. In the event that the dismissal of employees is mass in accordance with Article 48 of this Law, the employer shall notify the territorial body of the central executive authority, which implements the state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, about the planned dismissal of employees 10 calendar days before the dismissal, as well as within conducts consultations with trade unions for five calendar days on measures to prevent layoffs or reduce their number to a minimum or mitigate the adverse consequences of any layoffs;

